# iOS Speedflight

For safe local builds/tests, follow [apps/ios/AGENTS.md](../../apps/ios/AGENTS.md). iOS work or a build request alone does not authorize signing, distribution, commits, pushes, or external-skill installation.

Only for explicitly authorized publication, follow [docs/speedflight.md](../../docs/speedflight.md) before `scripts/speedflight.sh`. It signs, exports, and uploads in one invocation. Preserve the requested revision and the Tinkertanker (`PQ6U5ESLN2`) signing/device gates; use ASC-key preflight, not Xcode GUI sign-in as a proxy.

Keep install-page links in the authorized private chat only, never PRs/issues/public logs. If publication is blocked, report the unmet prerequisite; continue any independently authorized local validation.
